course: dictionary
lesson: 13312
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. Grill is one of these words. Look at the words around it to find the meaning the writer wants. «Dad let me help grill the sausages on the barbecue.» Here grill means to cook food with strong heat, and the barbecue is the clue.
explain: Grill can also be a thing, a part of a cooker. «The toast is under the grill.» The word under is a clue that grill means the metal part above or below the heat. Grill can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action).
explain: Sometimes grill is an action word for asking questions. «The police officer grilled the boy about where he had been.» Grilled means asked lots of hard questions, one after another. This is informal, so you will hear it in stories and talk more than in school writing.
explain: Always ask: does my meaning fit the sentence? Swap in your meaning and check. If it sounds silly, try another meaning.
fact: Grill is a noun (a grill) and a verb (to grill).
fact: «To grill» means to cook food on or under a grill, using strong heat.
fact: «A grill» can be a part of a cooker, or a frame of metal bars over heat.
fact: «A grill» can also be a metal grid over an opening, like on the front of a car. This is often spelled grille.
fact: «To grill someone» (informal) means to ask them lots of hard questions.
exercise: «We grilled the vegetables on the barbecue.» What does grilled mean here? | *Cooked with strong heat | Washed carefully | Put in a box | Asked lots of hard questions
exercise: «The car's grill was covered in mud.» What is the grill? | *A metal grid on the front of the car | A question someone asks | A kind of cooker | Hot food on a plate
exercise: «Never leave a grill alone when it is on.» In this sentence, what kind of word is grill? | A colour | An action, to cook food | *A thing, a part of a cooker | A question
test: «The detective grilled the suspect for two hours.» What does grilled mean here? | Hid under a table | *Asked lots of hard questions | Cooked on a barbecue | Ate very slowly
test: «Dad will grill the burgers at the park.» Which meaning is right? | A metal bar on a car | Put them in the bin | Ask them hard questions | *Cook them with strong heat from above or below
exam: «The grill of the oven was still hot, so Sam used tongs.» What does grill mean in this sentence? | A metal fence in a park | To wash a dish | *A part of a cooker, over or under the heat | To ask someone hard questions
